  "$comment": "Where an area is scrolled (PEN-175), written from packages/core/src/analytics/scroll.ts by packages/core/test/analytics-scroll.test.ts, which also checks it. `fraction`: [scrollTop, scrollHeight, clientHeight] and the position fractionOf gives (null: the area cannot scroll). `gate`: a ScrollGate run on a fake clock from 0; each step at its time moves the area to a position (null: it cannot scroll) or resets it (its content changed); `recorded` is each position the gate records, and when. `values` (PEN-177): the same gate holding any value (a cursor’s block, a selection as block, chars and span, a field’s length), starting with nothing recorded, so a first 0 is recorded; values are the same when equal as JSON; a step may also flush (record what waits at once, inside the settle and the gap, a repeat still dropped) or mark a value (known, not recorded; what waits is dropped). Kotlin’s ScrollEvents replays every case.",
